JA4 / JA4+ (TLS fingerprinting) -- SPLIT LICENSE, READ THIS
-------------------------------------------------------

The `foxio/ja4-zeek-scripts` package implements the JA4+ suite, which is
dual-licensed. Weirvern uses ONE member of it:

  JA4  (TLS client fingerprint)  BSD 3-Clause. Free for any use, including
       commercial. Copyright (c) 2026 FoxIO. Redistribution requires retaining
       this notice.
       License: https://github.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/blob/main/LICENSE-JA4

  JA4+ (JA4S, JA4H, JA4X, JA4SSH, JA4T, JA4L, JA4D, ...)  FoxIO License 1.1.
       Permissive for academic and internal business use, NOT permissive for
       monetization. Methods are patent pending.
       License: https://github.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/blob/main/LICENSE

Weirvern ships JA4 only, and ships it as SOURCE (the package is installed into
the sensor image at build time, not vendored into this repository). Shipping only
JA4 is a deliberate decision: the FoxIO FAQ states that a company using JA4+ "to
provide value to paying customers, even without exposing JA4+ fingerprints
directly to those customers, ... would still need an OEM license as they are
indirectly monetizing JA4+." Since Weirvern is intended to be deployable as a
product, enabling any JA4+ member would require an OEM license.

The package is installed whole (we cannot install half of it), but every
FoxIO-licensed submodule is disabled in k8s/zeek/weirvern-local.zeek. That
disable is ORDER-DEPENDENT: the package gates submodules with
`@if (JA4S_enabled) @load ./ja4s @endif`, and `@if` is evaluated when the file
is LOADED, so disabling the options after loading the package is silently
ignored and the fields still populate. See zeek/JA4-NOTICE and the tests in
tests/test_ja4_licensing.py, which assert the ORDER rather than mere presence.

If you enable any JA4+ member, you are responsible for holding an appropriate
FoxIO license.

